when West Edge revitalization is kind of an anchor um it tells a very very important story um about our history of our water management in the city and uh so we uh made a recommendation with a unanimous motion for the finance committee we thought it was important we also share it with the full governing body so I'll read it to you this was a motion passed by the Historic Preservation Board at its regular meeting on June 9th we the members of the Cheyenne Historic Preservation Board recommend that the original pump house structure be preserved and not put into surplus however if the building is put into surplus and put up for sale we recommend that the city put conditions on the sale and

also conditioned in the deed requiring that the structure number one not be demolished number two that the exterior of the structure is not altered to the point that it's rendered ineligible for listing in the National Register of Historic Places and number three that any renovations follow the US Department of the Interior's standards for historic preservation it's also come to light working with the planning department that this building uh may be uh eligible for listing in the National Register with some of the additions perhaps uh mitigated or removed if that is the case and uh the governing body decides to put this up for sale or put it into surplus and those conditions prevail it may avail future owner of the historic preservation tax credit which would give them a 20 uh% or or a credit on 20% of the cost of any restoration that they would invest into that property uh

overall um it's I think it's clear to you where we stand um the city of Cheyenne prides itself obviously on our history and we have leveraged that history for uh economic development um through uh obviously the most important obvious example being Frontier Days the pump house um should also follow that model that successful long-term model of leveraging our history uh for our betterment of our community and for economic impact thank you thanks for your service with the board thank you mr buyers welcome sir thank you Mayor uh Randy Buyers 1610 Pioneer Avenue um first of all I'd like to thank the city and I I know Mayor Collins you have put considerable effort into looking for potential tenants for the for the reuse and

